WEBVTT

00:16:59.935 --> 00:17:03.496
we are not going to go back
to the way it was.

00:17:04.173 --> 00:17:07.410
CA: So do you see systemic threats
to the financial industry

00:17:07.434 --> 00:17:10.434
as great or greater than happened in 2008?

00:17:11.736 --> 00:17:14.950
RD: Yeah, this is bigger
than what happened in 2008.

00:17:14.974 --> 00:17:16.181
I'll distinguish it.

00:17:16.205 --> 00:17:20.029
In 2008, we had banks.

00:17:20.688 --> 00:17:22.125
It's the same thing, meaning,

00:17:22.149 --> 00:17:23.982
you have a certain amount of leverage,

00:17:24.006 --> 00:17:25.609
things go down,

00:17:25.633 --> 00:17:29.442
too much leverage means you're broke,
in accounting terms.

00:17:29.466 --> 00:17:31.744
So then you look around and you say,